# Raw upstream catalogues — regenerable via fetch.py, and large. Deliberately
# not committed: they are minified single-line JSON that churns nightly, so git
# would store a fresh multi-MB blob every day for no diffing benefit. The
# nightly workflow passes them between jobs as artifacts and caches them across
# runs instead.
raw/

# The catalogue and the price ledger. They are still version-controlled, and
# still for the original reason — git is the database history, the backup and
# the audit log, for nothing — but in the private data repo, because this one
# is public. Keep in step with scripts/private-paths.txt, which is the list
# both sync scripts read and the place the reasoning is written down.
#
# The line being drawn: this repo is the crawler and the site, and both are
# fine to read. The catalogue is the product, and the price history is the one
# part of it that cannot be regenerated at any price — it accrues only by
# observing, daily. That is what is worth not publishing.
data/brands-master.json
data/bags.json
data/price-history.jsonl
data/price-state.json
data/enrich-cache.json
data/rejected.json
data/image-bg.json
data/fetch-log.json
data/collections/

# Run logs
data/*.out
# This run's price drops, handed to the alert matcher. Not a durable artifact —
# price-history.jsonl is the ledger.
data/price-events.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Astro / Vercel
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.vercel/
.env
.env.*.local

# Grove project metadata — local tooling config, not part of the build.
.grove/
# Codex hooks — same story, and the generated file hardcodes an absolute
# checkout path and a session id, so it is machine-specific besides.
.codex/

# Development page cache — raw brand pages kept so parser changes can be
# re-applied without re-crawling. Local working files, never published: they
# contain brands' full marketing copy, which the index deliberately does not
# reproduce.
data/page-cache/

# The gate's baseline, copied from the pulled catalogue before normalize.py
# writes over it. A build artefact of one run, never a record.
data/bags.baseline.json
.vercel
.env*
# The template carries no values and is the documentation for what .env needs.
!.env.template
